From a30b9627689926c8b620ff284df335c166f9ec7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:38:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(build): MAINT-02 - the service needs Node 22.6 and the
 devcontainer pins 20
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`pnpm test:render-api`, which I added in MAINT-01 and said would work, does not
work. It answers:

    node: bad option: --experimental-strip-types

I verified that script on a Node 22.22 machine and did not check what this
repository declares. .devcontainer/devcontainer.json pins `node:20-bookworm`,
and --experimental-strip-types arrived in Node 22.6. It was never going to run.

THE SCRIPT IS THE SMALL HALF. The service itself is TypeScript that Node strips
at load time, so its `start` script, both its test files and register.mjs all
need 22.6 — which means services/render-api cannot be run or tested at all in
this repository's own declared development environment. That is a RENDER-01
defect, not a MAINT-01 one; MAINT-01 only made it visible by adding a command
that hits it.

What is NOT affected, checked rather than assumed: the Dockerfile pins
node:24-slim, so the image this deploys from has had the feature for two major
versions and production is fine. Nothing else in the tree uses the flag — the
66 guards, parse-scan and the Next build are plain JavaScript or go through
Next's own compiler. The blast radius is exactly this service, run locally.

So the commands now say the one thing that is wrong. scripts/render-api-test.mjs
is plain JavaScript, so it starts on any Node, checks the version first, and
prints the versions side by side with the two ways forward. It exits 1 rather
than passing quietly. Both package.json scripts route through it, and the
service declares `engines: { node: ">=22.6.0" }` so the requirement is written
where somebody looks for it.

The two ways forward are stated and neither is taken here. Running it in
node:24-slim under Docker needs nothing installed, because the service has no
dependencies. Raising the devcontainer to node:22-bookworm is the tidier
answer and is a change to everyone's environment — including anything else
working in this repository — so it is a decision to be made rather than a side
effect of a patch, and I cannot run an install here to prove the rest of the
stack is happy on 22.

One fact worth having when that decision gets made: Node 20 left maintenance in
April 2026. It is already out of support.

65 of 66 guards here; verify:css needs an install. parse-scan clean on 642
files. Both service suites pass on Node 22.22, and the version gate was
exercised at a simulated Node 20.11.1 and exits 1 with the message above.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Wz3f94TUzSk49wD2izgQYx
